diff --git a/docs/design.md b/docs/design.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..caa8398
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/design.md
@@ -0,0 +1,100 @@
+# Design: pre-generated message ids and persistence status on `done`
+
+## Goal
+
+Clients streaming a chat turn should know the ids of the user and assistant
+messages from the very first event, and learn from the final `done` event whether
+the turn was saved — without a trailing `error` event. The answer is always
+delivered, even when saving fails.
+
+## Scope
+
+Included (backend only):
+
+- `ChatService.open_turn` pre-generates the two message ids (with `new_id`) and the
+  `ChatSession` exposes them as read-only properties.
+- `build_turn_messages` receives the ids instead of generating them.
+- The `conversation` event carries `message_id` (assistant id).
+- The `done` event carries `message_id` (assistant id, or `None` if saving failed),
+  `persisted` and `created_at` (ISO timestamp of the stored assistant message).
+- `ChatTurnResult` gains `user_message_id`, `assistant_message_id`, `created_at`.
+- Removal of `EventType.ERROR`, `ProgressEvent.error`, `ErrorCode.PERSIST_FAILED`
+  and `PERSIST_FAILED_MESSAGE`; no event follows `done`.
+- CLI `_render` prints `!! Không lưu được lượt hội thoại này.` to stderr on a
+  `done` event with `persisted` false; nothing to stderr otherwise for `done`.
+- README note on the SSE contract.
+
+Unchanged: the runner and graph, the domain `Message`/`Conversation` models, the
+repository port and adapters, the HTTP routes and their paths, the
+conversation `title`/`created` fields, existing `done` fields (`status`,
+`conversation_id`, runner data), `ChatTurnResult.message_id` semantics
+(assistant id or `None`), the assistant `created_at` offset rule.
+
+## Interfaces
+
+```python
+# pharma_agent.domain.conversation.turns
+def build_turn_messages(
+    *, conversation_id: str, run: AgentRun, answer_text: str,
+    citations: Sequence[Citation], phases: Sequence[str], now: datetime,
+    user_message_id: str, assistant_message_id: str,
+) -> tuple[Message, Message]
+
+# pharma_agent.application.chat.service
+class ChatTurnResult(BaseModel):
+    ...existing fields...
+    user_message_id: str
+    assistant_message_id: str
+    created_at: datetime          # == stored assistant message created_at
+
+class ChatSession:
+    def __init__(self, execution, conversation, *, created, conversations, clock,
+                 user_message_id: str, assistant_message_id: str) -> None
+    @property
+    def user_message_id(self) -> str
+    @property
+    def assistant_message_id(self) -> str
+
+# pharma_agent.application.progress
+class EventType(StrEnum):  # ERROR removed
+class ProgressEvent:       # error() classmethod removed
+
+# pharma_agent.domain.agent.run
+class ErrorCode(StrEnum):  # PERSIST_FAILED removed
+```
+
+Event payloads:
+
+- `conversation`: `{conversation_id, title, created, message_id}`
+- `done`: `{...runner data, conversation_id, message_id: str | None, persisted: bool, created_at: str}`
+
+## Approach
+
+- Ids are generated in the application layer (`ChatService.open_turn`) via the
+  shared `new_id` helper and handed to `ChatSession`; the domain function
+  `build_turn_messages` becomes a pure builder fed with ids, so it no longer
+  imports `new_id`.
+- `ChatSession._persist` passes the session's ids to `build_turn_messages`, and
+  fills the new `ChatTurnResult` fields; `created_at` is the assistant message's
+  `created_at` (now + 1µs) regardless of persistence outcome.
+- `ChatSession.events` builds the `done` event from the result: `message_id`,
+  `persisted`, `created_at.isoformat()`; nothing is yielded after it.
+- The SSE serializer and REST `POST /chat` need no change: they serialize event
+  data / `ChatTurnResult` as-is (the OpenAPI schema picks up the new fields).
+- CLI: replace the `ERROR` branch of `_render` with a `DONE` branch checking
+  `event.data.get("persisted") is False`. The CLI drives the runner directly,
+  whose `done` has no `persisted` key, so it stays silent there.
+
+## Testing
+
+- Domain: `build_turn_messages` uses the given ids (`tests/domain/test_conversation.py`).
+- Application: session exposes distinct ids; the `conversation` event carries the
+  assistant id; `done` carries `message_id`, `persisted=True`, `created_at`
+  matching the stored message; result fields match the stored messages; on
+  persist failure `done` is last with `message_id=None`, `persisted=False`, and
+  the answer is still present (`tests/application/test_chat_service.py`).
+- Progress contract: `EventType` has no `error`; `ErrorCode` has no `PERSIST_FAILED`.
+- API: stream `done` includes `persisted`/`created_at` (`tests/api/test_chat_api.py`).
+- CLI: `_render` prints the warning to stderr only for `persisted: False`
+  (`tests/test_cli.py`).
+- Full backend suite: `uv run pytest` from `backend/`.
